# Licence for the specification

`SPECIFICATION.md` in this directory is licensed under the
**Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International** licence (CC BY 4.0).

    https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/
    Full text: https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/legalcode

You may copy, redistribute, adapt and build on it, for any purpose including
commercially, as long as you give credit.

## Implementing the protocol needs no permission

To be explicit, because a licence on a document is not the same thing as
permission to implement what it describes:

**Anyone may implement this protocol, in any language, under any licence, open
source or not, without asking and without owing anything to this project.**

The reference implementation is under the AGPL. That licence applies to *that
code*. It does not reach an independent implementation written from this
document, and it is not meant to.

This is not generosity. Principle 1 says the network must not depend on any
particular person or organisation, and a protocol that only one codebase is
allowed to speak is that codebase's private protocol. An interoperable
implementation by someone else is the principle working.

## Trademarks are still separate

Implementing the protocol does not grant any right to the project's name or
marks. Keep the protocol identifiers — `/ovn/kad/1.0.0`, the gossip topics, the
`ourvideo://` scheme — because interoperating requires them. Do not call your
implementation Open Video Network. See [`../TRADEMARK.md`](../TRADEMARK.md).
